From: Paullo9 <paullobpreis@icloud.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 11:17:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] number-density-test/run.sh says why it does not source
 sources.manifest (inventory's harness rule; tier 3, comment)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 tools/number-density-test/run.sh | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tools/number-density-test/run.sh b/tools/number-density-test/run.sh
index f74ca5fd..94b4f10c 100755
--- a/tools/number-density-test/run.sh
+++ b/tools/number-density-test/run.sh
@@ -14,7 +14,8 @@ trap 'rm -rf "$WORK"' EXIT
 . "$REPO/tools/lib/developer-dir.sh"
 resolve_mac4dstem_developer_dir
 
-# Foundation only: the three precipitate files plus FloatImage's file (as tools/volumetric-density-test).
+# Does not source tools/lib/sources.manifest: it takes four named files, not a group. Foundation only: the three
+# precipitate files plus FloatImage's file (as tools/volumetric-density-test).
 xcrun swiftc -O -package-name mac4DSTEM -parse-as-library -swift-version 5 \
   -o "$WORK/nv" \
   main.swift \
